{title: 018 - O Morning Star, How Fair and Bright}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #018 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 18}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O Morning [A/C#]Star, how fair [D]and bright!
[Bm]You shine with [A/E]God's own truth [D]and light,
[Em]Aglow with grace [A]and mercy!
[D]Of Jacob's [G]race, King David's [A7/E]son,
[D/F#]Our Lord and [A]Master, You [D]have won
[Em]Our hearts to serve [A]You only!
[D]Lowly, holy!
[G]Great and Glorious, [F#m]all victorious,
[D]Rich in blessing! Rule [A]and might o'er [D]all possessing!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Lord, when you [A/C#]look on us [D]in love,
[Bm]At once there [A/E]falls from God [D]above
[Em]A ray of purest [A]pleasure.
[D]Your Word and [G]Spirit, flesh [A7/E]and blood,
[D/F#]Refresh our [A]souls with heav-'nly [D]food.
[Em]You are our dearest [A]treasure!
[D]Let Your mercy warm and cheer us!
[G]O draw near [F#m]us! For You [Em]teach us
[D]God's own love [A]through You has [D]reached us.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Almighty [A/C#]Father, in [D]Your Son
[Bm]You loved us, [A/E]when not yet [D]begun
[Em]Was this old earth's [A]foundation!
[D]Your Son has [G]ransomed us [A7/E]in love
[D/F#]To live in [A]Him here and [D]above:
[Em]This is Your great [A]salvation.
[D]Alleluia! Christ the living,
[G]To us giving [F#m]life forever,
[D]Keeps us Yours [A]and fails us [D]never!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]O let the [A/C#]harps break forth [D]in sound!
[Bm]Our joy be [A/E]all with music [D]crowned,
[Em]Our voices gaily [A]blending!
[D]For Christ goes [G]with us all [A7/E]the way '
[D/F#]Today, tomorrow, [A]every [D]day!
[D/F#]His love is [A]never [D]ending!
[Em]Sing out! [A]Ring out!
[D]Jubilation! Exultation!
[G]Tell the [F#m]story!
[D]Great is He, [A]the King of [D]glory!
{end_of_verse}
